<title>SPAIN: Telefonica, Sogecable end Cablevision deal.</title>
<headline>Telefonica, Sogecable end Cablevision deal.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish telephone operator Telefonica said on Friday that it and Sogecable ended on Thursday their participation in Cablevision.</p>
<p>Cablevision is a joint venture set up by Telefonica and Sogecable SA, a unit of Promotora de Informaciones SA (PRISA) and Canal Plus in July 1995 to operate and distribute pay television and multimedia in Spain via cable TV networks.</p>
<p>Cablevision now becomes 100 percent owned by Sogecable and Telefonica will take up the shares that Sogecable and Cablevision had in local operators.</p>
<p>The exception is the local operator in the Canary Islands, where Sogecable maintains an 11 percent stake, Telefonica said.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
